# Scryfall card cache: since the migration to SQLite (Step 4 of
# roadmap.md) it lives in the DB, so the legacy JSON no longer
# needs tracking. It can stay on disk as a local backup/migration fallback: the
# bot neither reads nor writes it once the cached_cards table is populated.
data/card_cache.json

# "Last lastmod seen" state for the Arena Event Schedule pages (utils/arena_event_schedule.py):
# pure operational bookkeeping to avoid reprocessing pages already notified, no editorial value
# to track in git (unlike arena_rarity_data.json, which holds hand-curated overrides).
data/arena_event_schedule_state.json

# Same for the "last lastmod seen" state of the Banned and Restricted Announcements
# (utils/ban_announcement.py) - pure bookkeeping, no editorial value.
data/ban_announcement_state.json

